From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:57:49 +0200
Subject: [M150-LTS][scopes] Restore synthetic eval heritage skip bit from
 inner scope

When Scope::DeserializeScopeChain injects a synthetic EVAL_SCOPE for a
context-less eval, DeclarationScope::RecalcPrivateNameContextChain has
already propagated private_name_lookup_skips_outer_class down to its
first child scope (or to ParseInfo flags if no inner scope allocated a
ScopeInfo). Reading the skip bit from the weak top-level eval SFI in
script->infos()[kFunctionLiteralIdTopLevel] loses the bit once GC
collects the eval's top-level SFI, causing lazy compilation of functions
inside a class heritage eval to bind private names to the inner class.

Restore private_name_lookup_skips_outer_class on the synthetic
EVAL_SCOPE from current_scope (and clear it on current_scope) or from
parse_info->flags(), and ensure DoParseFunction marks the function scope
with RecordNeedsPrivateNameContextChainRecalc() when the flag is set.

